    "body": "## Security impact\n\nPrivate live-tracking access loaded a job globally by numeric `jobId`, checked whether tracking was active, and only then checked whether the caller was the requester or assigned worker. An authenticated outsider could therefore distinguish:\n\n- nonexistent jobs (`404`),\n- existing jobs without active tracking (`409`), and\n- existing jobs with active tracking (`403`).\n\nThat creates an existence and lifecycle oracle over private accepted jobs in the most sensitive location/GPS surface.\n\n## Fix\n\n- resolve tracking access through the existing participant-scoped `JobRepository.findParticipantById(jobId, userId)` query;\n- reject a missing/non-participant match with one neutral `403` before checking tracking status;\n- fail closed before repository access when the authenticated principal has no persisted user id;\n- preserve participant semantics: owner/worker still receive lifecycle conflicts for inactive tracking, assigned workers can publish GPS, and the requester still cannot publish worker location.\n\nThe neutral response remains `403`, matching the established runtime contract while removing the distinguishing signal: outsiders now receive the same response for active, inactive, and nonexistent job IDs.\n\n## Tests\n\nAdded focused `LiveTrackingAccessServiceTest` coverage for:\n\n- outsider/missing-job indistinguishability through participant-scoped lookup;\n- missing authenticated identity failing closed without repository access;\n- participant lifecycle conflict after successful ownership resolution;\n- requester viewing active tracking;\n- assigned worker publishing active tracking;\n- requester being forbidden from publishing worker GPS.\n\nNo GPS coordinates, ETA calculation, tracking retention, rate limiting, checkpoint validation, or settlement logic is changed.\n\n## Merge gate\n\nMerge only after all relevant checks on the exact PR head are green, `master` is revalidated and has not moved (or the branch is safely rebased), then merge with a merge commit using the exact checked head SHA. Verify post-merge master workflows before starting another slice.",
